# Orders CLI

When the task involves **inspecting order/inventory/fulfilment state or running an admin mutation** (refund, release-reservation, resend-confirmation, create-shipment), prefer `npm run orders` over raw Supabase SQL, ad-hoc scripts, or the Cloudflare-Access-gated `/admin` UI.

```bash
npm run orders -- [--env-file .dev.vars] [--compact] <resource> <action>
```

Reference: `docs/orders-cli.md` (commands, safety guards, exit codes, smoke test).

## Use the CLI for

- Merged order inspection (`order get <uuid>` — order + line items, `piece_state`, `prodigi_orders`/`fulfilment_jobs`, Stripe PaymentIntent summary)
- Order/inventory listing and filtering (`order list`, `inventory list`)
- Running the four admin mutations from a terminal/agent session instead of the gated `/admin` UI: `order refund`, `order release-reservation`, `order resend-confirmation`, `order create-shipment`

## Do not use the CLI for

- Replacing automated tests (`src/lib/admin/actions.test.ts` / `scripts/orders-cli.test.ts` mock Supabase/Stripe/InPost; the CLI makes real requests)
- Pure storefront/UI work with no order/admin data surface

## Safety defaults

- Keys from `.env.local` → `.dev.vars` → `--env-file` → `process.env` (same precedence as `prodigi-cli`)
- Reads work against whatever Supabase project is loaded — no target guard
- Every mutation requires `--confirm <order-id>` matching the target id exactly
- Mutations are blocked against a non-production Supabase project unless `--allow-nonprod` is passed
- PII (email, name, phone, address) is redacted by default; use `--show-pii` only when operationally necessary
- Adding a fifth admin mutation? Add it to `src/lib/admin/actions.ts` first (dependency-injected clients) so the `/api/admin/*` route and the CLI call the same function — do not duplicate the logic in the route and the CLI separately
